@ 37.2.6.3 - Proto-Dhegiha to Osage
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan I”. International Journal
# 			of American Linguistics 16(2):61 – 66; Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan II”
# 			International Journal of American Linguistics 16(3):113 – 121; Wolff, Hans (1950),
# 			“Comparative Siouan III”. International Journal of American Linguistics 16(4):168 – 178;
# 			and cedh audmanh’s changes above, which assisted me in deciphering the vintage phonetic
# 			transcription scheme
	# NB: Does not include developments in unstressed non-nasal vowels. L was apparently
	# 			either /ɹ/ or /l/; Lʲ (Lʸ in the text) was apparently /j/, or maybe /ʎ/.
	p > {p,b,m,w} / _C
	t > t͡s / _E
	s > θ
	{ç,x} > z
	n > ð / _{ã,ẽ,õ}
	w > b / #_
	Lʲ > ð / _V:[+nas -stress]
	ʔ > ∅ / p_
	t > t͡s / _ʔ
	pr sr tʲr kr > bð sts ʃd ɡð
	r > ð / x_
	m > ∅ / #_n
	mn > bð / {C,V}_{C,V}
	sn mt > hn d
	ʃ > s / ”V_k
	xk > (ʃ)k / _”V
	xk > ɡ / ”V_
	x > ʔ / k_”V